# type(scope): step N - what changed, in plain words
#
# The why, as one or two paragraphs wrapped at about 85:
#   What it means first, for someone who uses it.
#   Then what changed, and why this design and not the others:
#   the pattern, the ADR, Louis's pick in his own words, quoted.
#   For a fix: what was seen, and its cause.
#   Then the tests: which was seen failing first, what was checked
#   by eye, and what was not checked.
#
# ---- The first line -------------------------------------------------
#   type    feat | fix | refactor | test | docs
#   scope   the id in lowercase: f22, fx14, cl3, f49.1
#           or the area when there is none: ollama, guide
#   step N  only on a plan's steps: "step 3 - "
#   e.g.    feat(f22): step 3 - ReadTable for spreadsheets
#           fix(fx14): the prompt budget counts cached tokens
#
# ---- Never ----------------------------------------------------------
#   No Co-Authored-By, and no other line that names Claude.
#   No author but Louis Marais <84603591+bosbevk@users.noreply.github.com>.
#
# Lines starting with # are dropped by git. The rest is in /ship-it.
